    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 15,
    "summary": "A soft answer turns away wrath—A wise son makes a glad father—The thoughts of the wicked are an abomination to the Lord—Before honor comes humility.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Patience; Self-Mastery."
          },
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Communication."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "Gen. 26:22 (17–22)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The tongue of the wise useth knowledge aright: but the mouth of fools poureth out foolishness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Communication."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG Foolishness; Gossip."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The eyes of the Lord are in every place, beholding the evil and the good.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG God, Omniscience of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wholesome tongue is a tree of life: but perverseness therein is a breach in the spirit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Honesty; Profanity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A fool despiseth his father’s instruction: but he that regardeth reproof is prudent.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "Prov. 10:1; D&C 68:31."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Prov. 13:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the house of the righteous is much treasure: but in the revenues of the wicked is trouble.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The lips of the wise disperse knowledge: but the heart of the foolish doeth not so.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Communication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination to the Lord: but the prayer of the upright is his delight.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Gen. 4:5; Moro. 7:8 (5–11). TG Sacrifice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 91
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The way of the wicked is an abomination unto the Lord: but he loveth him that followeth after righteousness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Correction is grievous unto him that forsaketh the way: and he that hateth reproof shall die.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "1 Ne. 16:2; 2 Ne. 1:26; 9:40; Mosiah 13:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "TG Reproof."
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "Prov. 14:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Hell and destruction are before the Lord: how much more then the hearts of the children of men?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A scorner loveth not one that reproveth him: neither will he go unto the wise.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A merry heart maketh a cheerful countenance: but by sorrow of the heart the spirit is broken.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Happiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Prov. 17:22."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "TG Cheerful."
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Sorrow."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The heart of him that hath understanding seeketh knowledge: but the mouth of fools feedeth on foolishness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Prov. 14:6. TG Knowledge."
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 105,
            "text": "TG Foolishness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "All the days of the afflicted are evil: but he that is of a merry heart hath a continual feast.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Better is little with the fear of the Lord than great treasure and trouble therewith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Ps. 37:16; Eccl. 4:6; James 2:5 (1–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Better is a dinner of herbs where love is, than a stalled ox and hatred therewith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "Prov. 17:1. TG Love."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "IE fattened ox."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wrathful man stirreth up strife: but he that is slow to anger appeaseth strife.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Prov. 14:29."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Contention."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The way of the slothful man is as an hedge of thorns: but the way of the righteous is made plain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 85
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish man despiseth his mother.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Prov. 10:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Motherhood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Folly is joy to him that is destitute of wisdom: but a man of understanding walketh uprightly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Without counsel purposes are disappointed: but in the multitude of counsellors they are established.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:28; Jacob 4:10; Alma 37:12; D&C 105:37; 122:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man hath joy by the answer of his mouth: and a word spoken in due season, how good is it!",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "Prov. 25:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Eccl. 3:1 (1–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 60
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 91
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The way of life is above to the wise, that he may depart from hell beneath.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Col. 3:2; 2 Ne. 9:39."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord will destroy the house of the proud: but he will establish the border of the widow.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "Prov. 12:7; D&C 64:24."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Ps. 146:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The thoughts of the wicked are an abomination to the Lord: but the words of the pure are pleasant words.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 72
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 88
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that is greedy of gain troubleth his own house; but he that hateth gifts shall live.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The heart of the righteous studieth to answer: but the mouth of the wicked poureth out evil things.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Study."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Communication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord is far from the wicked: but he heareth the prayer of the righteous.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Ps. 10:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Mosiah 11:24 (23–25); 21:15; D&C 101:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The light of the eyes rejoiceth the heart: and a good report maketh the bones fat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 46
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The ear that heareth the reproof of life abideth among the wise.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that refuseth instruction despiseth his own soul: but he that heareth reproof getteth understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "OR obeys."
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of the Lord is the instruction of wisdom; and before honour is humility.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "TG Honor."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Humility."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
